<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Plessey year EPS falls, div held.</title>
<headline>Plessey year EPS falls, div held.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		 (millions of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>Shr</p>
<p>    - weighted av(cts)  30.0   vs  41.5</p>
<p>    - diluted	     28.0   vs  40.6</p>
<p>    Yr div		  13.0   vs  13.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 41.44  vs 51.31</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 50.95  vs 81.42</p>
<p>    Tax			8.05  vs 31.24</p>
<p>Revenue from</p>
<p>    continuing ops    1,033.71 vs 793.13</p>
<p>Revenue from</p>
<p>    discontinued ops    280.47 vs 276.49</p>
<p>Loss on sale of</p>
<p>    discontinued ops	8.51 vs nil</p>
<p>Div payment to be announced</p>
<p>On register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: Plessey Corporation Ltd (electronics)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that after the sale of its consumer electronics division, it was confident that its other operations would be able to restore profitability to satisfying levels.</p>
<p>Shareholders will be able to choose to receive capitalisation shares in lieu of the dividend.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
